      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a professional social media content strategist.\n\nUSER BRIEF:\n{{ $('Telegram Trigger').first().json.message.text }}\n\nRead the user's brief and identify the content idea, target audience, and brand tone.\n\nGenerate a 7-day social media content plan based on the user's main idea.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Generate exactly 7 sections: DAY 1 through DAY 7.\n- Each day must have a unique topic related to the original idea.\n- Each day must contain a LinkedIn post, an X thread of 4 connected posts, and an Instagram caption.\n- Do not invent facts, statistics, or unsupported claims.\n- Return the actual written content, not placeholders.\n- Do not return JSON, Markdown tables, or introductory text.\n\nUse these exact headings and this exact structure for every day:\n\nDAY 1\nTopic: [topic]\n\nLinkedIn Post:\n[Complete LinkedIn post]\n\nX Thread:\n1/4 [Post 1]\n2/4 [Post 2]\n3/4 [Post 3]\n4/4 [Post 4]\n\nInstagram Caption:\n[Complete Instagram caption with relevant hashtags]\n\nRepeat this structure for DAY 2, DAY 3, DAY 4, DAY 5, DAY 6, and DAY 7.\n\nDo not comit any day or platform. Keep each platform heading on a separate line. Replace all bracketed instructions with actual content.",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a professional social media content strategist. Always return three clearly labelled drafts: LinkedIn, X (Twitter) and Instagram."
        }
      },
      "id": "90e0e23a-7a4f-4bcc-a4bd-6cd4a3326e36",
      "name": "AI Agent",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        496,
        528
      ],
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "\nconst data = $input.first().json;\n\n// 1. AI Agent output\nconst output = String(\n  data.output ?? data.text ?? data.response ?? \"\"\n).trim();\n\nif (!output) {\n  throw new Error(\n    \"AI Agent output empty hai. Input check karein.\"\n  );\n}\n\n// 2. Original Telegram brief\nconst brief = String(\n  $(\"Telegram Trigger\").first().json.message?.text ?? \"\"\n);\n\n// 3. Brief fields\nfunction getBriefField(labels) {\n  for (const label of labels) {\n    const regex = new RegExp(\n      \"^\\\\s*\" + label + \"\\\\s*:\\\\s*(.+?)\\\\s*$\",\n      \"im\"\n    );\n\n    const match = brief.match(regex);\n    if (match) return match[1].trim();\n  }\n\n  return \"\";\n}\n\nconst idea =\n  getBriefField([\"Content Idea\", \"Idea\", \"Topic\"]) ||\n  \"Not provided\";\n\nconst audience =\n  getBriefField([\"Target Audience\", \"Audience\", \"Target\"]) ||\n  \"Not provided\";\n\nconst tone =\n  getBriefField([\"Brand Tone\", \"Tone\", \"Brand Voice\"]) ||\n  \"Not provided\";\n\n// 4. Normalize AI output\nconst text = output.replace(/\\\\n/g, \"\\n\");\n\n// 5. Find DAY 1 to DAY 7\nconst dayRegex = /^\\s*DAY\\s+([1-7])\\s*:?\\s*$/gim;\n\nconst headings = [];\nlet match;\n\nwhile ((match = dayRegex.exec(text)) !== null) {\n  headings.push({\n    day: Number(match[1]),\n    start: match.index,\n    end: dayRegex.lastIndex\n  });\n}\n\n// Keep first occurrence of each day\nconst uniqueDays = [];\nconst seenDays = new Set();\n\nfor (const heading of headings) {\n  if (!seenDays.has(heading.day)) {\n    seenDays.add(heading.day);\n    uniqueDays.push(heading);\n  }\n}\n\nuniqueDays.sort((a, b) => a.day - b.day);\n\nif (\n  uniqueDays.length !== 7 ||\n  ![1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7].every(\n    day => seenDays.has(day)\n  )\n) {\n  throw new Error(\n    `Exactly DAY 1 to DAY 7 required. Found ${uniqueDays.length} unique days.`\n  );\n}\n\n// 6. Extract platform sections\nfunction extractSection(section, platform) {\n  const patterns = {\n    linkedin:\n      /^\\s*(?:\\*\\*)?\\s*LinkedIn(?:\\s+Post)?\\s*:?\\s*(?:\\*\\*)?\\s*/im,\n\n    x:\n      /^\\s*(?:\\*\\*)?\\s*(?:X|Twitter)(?:\\s+Thread)?\\s*:?\\s*(?:\\*\\*)?\\s*/im,\n\n    instagram:\n      /^\\s*(?:\\*\\*)?\\s*Instagram(?:\\s+Caption)?\\s*:?\\s*(?:\\*\\*)?\\s*/im\n  };\n\n  const found = patterns[platform].exec(section);\n  if (!found) return \"\";\n\n  const start = found.index + found[0].length;\n  const lines = section.slice(start).split(\"\\n\");\n  const contentLines = [];\n\n  const nextHeading =\n    /^\\s*(?:\\*\\*)?\\s*(?:LinkedIn(?:\\s+Post)?|(?:X|Twitter)(?:\\s+Thread)?|Instagram(?:\\s+Caption)?)\\s*:?\\s*(?:\\*\\*)?\\s*$/i;\n\n  for (const line of lines) {\n    if (nextHeading.test(line)) break;\n    contentLines.push(line);\n  }\n\n  return contentLines\n    .join(\"\\n\")\n    .trim()\n    .replace(/\\n{3,}/g, \"\\n\\n\");\n}\n\n// 7. Create seven rows with unique IDs\nconst executionId = String($execution.id);\n\nreturn uniqueDays.map(({ day }, index) => {\n  const currentIndex = uniqueDays.findIndex(\n    item => item.day === day\n  );\n\n  const heading = uniqueDays[currentIndex];\n  const next = uniqueDays[currentIndex + 1];\n\n  const section = text.slice(\n    heading.end,\n    next ? next.start : text.length\n  );\n\n  const linkedin = extractSection(section, \"linkedin\");\n  const xThread = extractSection(section, \"x\");\n  const instagram = extractSection(section, \"instagram\");\n\n  if (!linkedin || !xThread || !instagram) {\n    throw new Error(\n      `DAY ${day}: LinkedIn, X Thread, ya Instagram content missing hai.`\n    );\n  }\n\n  return {\n    json: {\n      Content_ID: `${executionId}-${day}`,\n      Content_Idea: idea,\n      Target_Audience: audience,\n      Brand_Tone: tone,\n      LinkedIn_Post: linkedin,\n      X_Thread: xThread,\n      Instagram_Caption: instagram,\n      Approval_Status: \"PENDING\",\n      Scheduled_Date: \"\",\n      Approved_At: \"\"\n    }\n  };\n});\n\n\n\n\n"
      },
